			<string>Params Template (optional)</string>
			<key>footerText</key>
			<string>Leave empty to send the default form fields (title, message, timestamp, sign).

The template format follows the Content-Type header (see Headers below): application/json or a template starting with '{' sends it as a JSON body; text/* sends it as a raw text body; anything else is sent as a form body (k1=v1&amp;k2=v2).

Placeholders are replaced with the notification data: [title] title, [sub] subtitle, [msg] message, [date] date, [app] app name, [appid] bundle ID, [device] device name, [icon] base64 icon, [image] base64 image, [key] auth value, [timestamp] current time in ms, [sign] HmacSHA256 signature. Values are escaped automatically.

JSON example: {"content": "[msg]"}
Form example: content=[msg]
GET query example: content=[msg] (a leading '/' makes it a path-style query).</string>
